<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0 -->
<TEI xmlns="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0" xmlns:rng="http://relaxng.org/ns/structure/1.0"
  xmlns:sch="http://purl.oclc.org/dsdl/schematron" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:lang="en">
  <teiHeader>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>The SOLEMNE Encoding Guidelines</title>
        <author>Gleb Schmidt</author>
        <author>Friederike Voit</author>
        <author>Sven Meeder</author>
      </titleStmt>
      <editionStmt>
        <edition n="0.4.0">Version 0.4.0</edition>
      </editionStmt>
      <publicationStmt>
        <publisher>SOLEMNE: The Social Life of Early Medieval Normative Texts, Radboud University</publisher>
        <availability>
          <licence target="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">This ODD, the guide: CC BY 4.0.</licence>
          <licence target="https://opensource.org/license/mit">The schema generated from it: MIT. It contains
            material of TEI P5 (the TEI Consortium: CC BY 3.0 and BSD 2-Clause), and its compiled Schematron the code
            of SchXslt2 (David Maus, MIT): their notices are at the top of each generated file.</licence>
        </availability>
      </publicationStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <p>Written for the project, on TEI P5. Its manuscript description is modelled on the Bodleian Libraries'
          consolidated TEI schema for manuscript descriptions.</p>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
    <encodingDesc>
      <classDecl>
        <taxonomy xml:id="tiers">
          <desc>The tiers: how far a file goes, from a minimal file to the full encoding. Every element, attribute
            and rule of the schema belongs to one tier, named by <att>corresp</att> on its specification, or, for an
            element taken from TEI unchanged, by the table of elements beside the specification.</desc>
          <category xml:id="tier-required">
            <catDesc><term>required</term>: what every file has. A file without it fails the checks: the import
              refuses a file that fails the RelaxNG, and reports the Schematron's errors, such as a formal title
              without the document's code.</catDesc>
          </category>
          <category xml:id="tier-common">
            <catDesc><term>common</term>: what most encoders add, as most of the project's coded files
              do.</catDesc>
          </category>
          <category xml:id="tier-full">
            <catDesc><term>full</term>: every other claim about the text, its source or the world, at full depth,
              signed and with its evidence.</catDesc>
          </category>
          <category xml:id="tier-export-only">
            <catDesc><term>export only</term>: the application's own state, which only its exports write, so that
              anyone can read them.</catDesc>
          </category>
        </taxonomy>
      </classDecl>
    </encodingDesc>
  </teiHeader>
  <text>
    <front>
      <!-- The title page of the HTML and the PDF. Its version and date are the release's: the edition's above, and
           the date of its section in the changelog. -->
      <titlePage>
        <docTitle>
          <titlePart type="main">The SOLEMNE Encoding Guidelines</titlePart>
        </docTitle>
        <docAuthor>Gleb Schmidt</docAuthor>
        <docAuthor>Friederike Voit</docAuthor>
        <docAuthor>Sven Meeder</docAuthor>
        <docEdition>Version 0.4.0</docEdition>
        <docDate when="2026-11-05">5 November 2026</docDate>
        <docImprint>SOLEMNE: The Social Life of Early Medieval Normative Texts, Radboud University, Nijmegen; funded by
          the European Research Council, grant 101087979. The guide is under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
          licence; the schema made from it, under the MIT licence.</docImprint>
      </titlePage>
      <xi:include href="chapters/introduction.xml"/>
    </front>
    <body>
      <xi:include href="chapters/what-a-file-describes.xml"/>
      <xi:include href="chapters/file-and-header.xml"/>
      <xi:include href="chapters/text.xml"/>
      <xi:include href="chapters/marked-in-the-text.xml"/>
      <xi:include href="chapters/records.xml"/>
      <xi:include href="chapters/relations.xml"/>
      <xi:include href="chapters/dates.xml"/>
      <xi:include href="chapters/manuscripts.xml"/>
      <xi:include href="chapters/editions-and-literature.xml"/>
      <xi:include href="chapters/exports.xml"/>

      <div xml:id="specification">
        <head>The specification</head>
        <p>The schema takes the modules of TEI below, and from each only the elements listed: an element outside
          them fails the RelaxNG. Each part's specifications follow, in the parts' order. An element the
          specifications change carries its tier there; the others take theirs from this table.</p>
        <table xml:id="element-tiers">
          <head>The elements taken from TEI unchanged, by tier</head>
          <row role="label">
            <cell>Tier</cell>
            <cell>Elements</cell>
          </row>
          <row corresp="#tier-required">
            <cell>required</cell>
            <cell>
              <gi>fileDesc</gi> <gi>publicationStmt</gi> <gi>sourceDesc</gi> <gi>TEI</gi> <gi>text</gi>
            </cell>
          </row>
          <row corresp="#tier-common">
            <cell>common</cell>
            <cell>
              <gi>address</gi> <gi>analytic</gi>
              <gi>distributor</gi> <gi>email</gi> <gi>forename</gi> <gi>imprint</gi> <gi>listPerson</gi>
              <gi>monogr</gi> <gi>p</gi> <gi>postCode</gi> <gi>publisher</gi> <gi>pubPlace</gi>
              <gi>series</gi> <gi>standOff</gi> <gi>street</gi> <gi>surname</gi>
            </cell>
          </row>
          <row corresp="#tier-full">
            <cell>full</cell>
            <cell>
              <gi>abbr</gi> <gi>abstract</gi> <gi>acquisition</gi> <gi>add</gi> <gi>additional</gi> <gi>additions</gi>
              <gi>addName</gi> <gi>addrLine</gi> <gi>adminInfo</gi> <gi>affiliation</gi> <gi>anchor</gi>
              <gi>authority</gi> <gi>availability</gi> <gi>bindingDesc</gi> <gi>birth</gi>
              <gi>bloc</gi> <gi>calendarDesc</gi> <gi>catDesc</gi> <gi>category</gi> <gi>choice</gi>
              <gi>cit</gi> <gi>classDecl</gi> <gi>collation</gi> <gi>colophon</gi>
              <gi>condition</gi> <gi>corr</gi> <gi>correction</gi> <gi>creation</gi> <gi>death</gi> <gi>decoDesc</gi>
              <gi>del</gi> <gi>depth</gi> <gi>desc</gi> <gi>district</gi> <gi>edition</gi> <gi>editionStmt</gi>
              <gi>encodingDesc</gi> <gi>expan</gi> <gi>explicit</gi> <gi>extent</gi> <gi>f</gi> <gi>finalRubric</gi>
              <gi>foliation</gi> <gi>foreign</gi> <gi>fs</gi> <gi>funder</gi> <gi>genName</gi> <gi>geo</gi>
              <gi>geogName</gi> <gi>graphic</gi> <gi>height</gi> <gi>hi</gi> <gi>history</gi> <gi>incipit</gi>
              <gi>interpretation</gi> <gi>item</gi> <gi>keywords</gi> <gi>label</gi> <gi>language</gi>
              <gi>langUsage</gi> <gi>layout</gi> <gi>layoutDesc</gi> <gi>lb</gi> <gi>licence</gi>
              <gi>listAnnotation</gi> <gi>listBibl</gi> <gi>listChange</gi> <gi>listEvent</gi> <gi>listOrg</gi>
              <gi>listPlace</gi> <gi>listPrefixDef</gi> <gi>listWit</gi> <gi>location</gi> <gi>locus</gi>
              <gi>locusGrp</gi> <gi>measure</gi> <gi>msContents</gi> <gi>msIdentifier</gi> <gi>msName</gi>
              <gi>name</gi> <gi>nameLink</gi> <gi>normalization</gi> <gi>notesStmt</gi> <gi>num</gi>
              <gi>occupation</gi> <gi>org</gi> <gi>orig</gi> <gi>origin</gi> <gi>physDesc</gi> <gi>place</gi>
              <gi>principal</gi> <gi>profileDesc</gi> <gi>projectDesc</gi> <gi>provenance</gi> <gi>punctuation</gi>
              <gi>q</gi> <gi>quotation</gi> <gi>recordHist</gi> <gi>refsDecl</gi> <gi>reg</gi> <gi>resp</gi>
              <gi>respStmt</gi> <gi>revisionDesc</gi> <gi>roleName</gi> <gi>rubric</gi> <gi>samplingDecl</gi>
              <gi>seriesStmt</gi> <gi>sic</gi> <gi>source</gi> <gi>sponsor</gi> <gi>stdVals</gi> <gi>subst</gi>
              <gi>summary</gi> <gi>supplied</gi> <gi>support</gi> <gi>surrogates</gi> <gi>taxonomy</gi> <gi>term</gi>
              <gi>textClass</gi> <gi>textLang</gi> <gi>unclear</gi> <gi>width</gi> <gi>witness</gi>
            </cell>
          </row>
          <row corresp="#tier-export-only">
            <cell>export only</cell>
            <cell>
              <gi>citeData</gi> <gi>citeStructure</gi> <gi>link</gi>
            </cell>
          </row>
        </table>
        <schemaSpec ident="solemne" start="TEI" docLang="en" targetLang="en" xml:id="element-outside-the-schema"
          corresp="#tier-required">

          <!-- The modules, and the elements taken from each. -->
          <moduleRef key="tei"/>
          <moduleRef key="core"
            include="abbr add addrLine address analytic author bibl biblScope biblStruct choice cit citedRange corr
              date del desc editor email expan foreign gap graphic head imprint item label lb list listBibl measure
              monogr name note num orig p pb postCode ptr publisher pubPlace q quote ref reg resp respStmt rs series sic
              street term textLang title unclear hi"/>
          <moduleRef key="header"
            include="abstract authority availability calendar calendarDesc catDesc category change citeData
              citeStructure classDecl correction creation distributor edition editionStmt editorialDecl encodingDesc
              extent fileDesc funder handNote idno interpretation keywords langUsage language licence listChange listPrefixDef normalization
              notesStmt prefixDef principal profileDesc projectDesc publicationStmt punctuation quotation refsDecl
              revisionDesc
              samplingDecl segmentation seriesStmt sourceDesc sponsor stdVals taxonomy teiHeader textClass
              titleStmt"/>
          <moduleRef key="textstructure" include="TEI body div text"/>
          <moduleRef key="namesdates"
            include="addName affiliation birth bloc country death district event eventName floruit forename genName
              geo geogName listEvent listOrg listPerson listPlace listRelation location nameLink occupation org
              orgName persName person place placeName region relation roleName settlement surname"/>
          <moduleRef key="msdescription"
            include="acquisition additional additions adminInfo altIdentifier binding bindingDesc collation collection
              colophon condition decoDesc decoNote depth dimensions explicit finalRubric foliation handDesc height
              history incipit institution layout layoutDesc locus locusGrp msContents msDesc msIdentifier msItem msName
              msPart objectDesc origDate origin origPlace physDesc provenance recordHist repository rubric source
              summary support supportDesc surrogates width"/>
          <moduleRef key="linking" include="anchor annotation link linkGrp listAnnotation seg standOff"/>
          <moduleRef key="transcr" include="subst supplied"/>
          <moduleRef key="textcrit" include="listWit witness"/>
          <moduleRef key="iso-fs" include="fs f"/>

          <!-- Each part's specifications, in the parts' order. -->
          <specGrpRef target="#header-title-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#header-pointers-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#header-encoding-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#header-external-ids-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#text-divisions-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#text-headings-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#text-page-breaks-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#text-gaps-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#marked-names-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#marked-works-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#marked-statements-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#marked-pointers-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#marked-notes-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#marked-other-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#records-persons-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#records-institutions-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#records-events-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#records-works-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#records-external-ids-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#relations-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#relations-types-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#dates-form-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#dates-calendars-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#dates-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#manuscripts-description-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#manuscripts-units-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#manuscripts-contents-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#manuscripts-physical-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#manuscripts-hands-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#manuscripts-decoration-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#manuscripts-binding-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#manuscripts-history-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#editions-pages-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#editions-biblatex-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#exports-annotations-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#exports-reuse-specs"/>
          <specGrpRef target="#exports-history-specs"/>

        </schemaSpec>
      </div>
    </body>
    <back>
      <!-- solemne-tei docs generates appendices A, B, C and F in place of these placeholders: A and B from the
           specifications, C from the package's code tables and the vocabularies' seeds, F from the changelog. -->
      <divGen xml:id="appendix-elements" type="elements">
        <head>The elements and attributes</head>
      </divGen>
      <divGen xml:id="appendix-rules" type="rules">
        <head>The rules</head>
      </divGen>
      <divGen xml:id="appendix-tables" type="tables">
        <head>The code tables and the vocabularies</head>
      </divGen>
      <div xml:id="appendix-older-forms">
        <head>Older encodings</head>
        <p>The project's files were encoded before this guide, after the old Solemne guide, and some of their forms
          have changed. The corrections bring the project's own files to the guide's forms; this table is for anyone
          reading a file in an older form. Each row gives the older form, what it became, and where the guide
          explains it.</p>
        <table xml:id="older-forms-table">
          <row role="label">
            <cell>The older form</cell>
            <cell>What it became</cell>
            <cell>Where</cell>
          </row>
          <row role="label">
            <cell cols="3">The header</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>The formal title's <gi>idno</gi> typed <val>collCode</val>, <val>collCat</val> and
              <val>collType</val></cell>
            <cell>an untyped <gi>idno</gi> for the code, <gi>idno</gi> typed <val>category</val> and
              <val>type</val></cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#header-title"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>The category <val>DP</val></cell>
            <cell><val>D</val></cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#header-categories"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>A date joined to a code by a dot: <code>P.THB.0700</code></cell>
            <cell>joined by a hyphen: <code>P.THB-0700</code></cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#header-codes"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><att>key</att> on <gi>title</gi>, <gi>author</gi>, <gi>origPlace</gi> and <gi>country</gi>;
              <att>corresp</att> on <gi>provenance</gi>; persons by short keys (<code>who="#GS"</code>)</cell>
            <cell><att>ref</att>, pointing to a record by a placeholder, an id in the file or a permalink; in
              <gi>provenance</gi>, on the name inside it</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#header-responsibility"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Clavis's keys as <att>xml:id</att>s</cell>
            <cell>in <att>sameAs</att>, with the <code>clavis</code> prefix declared in <gi>listPrefixDef</gi></cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#header-external-ids"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>The root's <att>xml:id</att> as the document's address (<code>collection_1234</code>); the
              document as one <gi>div</gi> typed <val>collection</val></cell>
            <cell>the document's code in the formal title; the <gi>body</gi> is the document</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#documents-and-nodes"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row role="label">
            <cell cols="3">The text's structure</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><gi>div</gi> typed <val>atomicUnit</val></cell>
            <cell><val>unit</val>, where several stand side by side; a lone one dissolves into its parent</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#text-units"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><gi>div</gi> typed <val>opener</val></cell>
            <cell>dissolved: its headings are the headings of the division it opens</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#text-headings"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><gi>div</gi> typed <val>chapterGroup</val>, and untyped divisions</cell>
            <cell><val>chapter</val>: a chapter may hold chapters</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#text-divisions"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><gi>div</gi> typed <val>part</val>, at the top</cell>
            <cell><val>section</val></cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#text-divisions"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>The old guide's division types: <val>canon</val>, <val>norm</val>, <val>authGrp</val>,
              <val>authStmt</val>, <val>authStmtGrp</val>, <val>decretal</val>, <val>registerCanon</val>,
              <val>romanLaw</val>, <val>act</val></cell>
            <cell>the closed list of division types</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#text-divisions"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>A file that is only a register, its items in the body</cell>
            <cell>one <gi>div</gi> typed <val>register</val> around its items</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#text-registers"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><gi>head</gi> typed <val>num</val></cell>
            <cell><val>number</val>, the division's number as a value in <att>n</att></cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#text-numbers"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><gi>head</gi> typed <val>inscriptio</val>; the old guide's <val>denom</val>,
              <val>highlight</val> and <val>paragr</val></cell>
            <cell><val>inscription</val> where the heading begins with its source, <val>rubric</val> where it begins
              with its subject</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#text-headings"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Misspelt types (<val>chpater</val>, <val>inscripto</val>, <val>atoimcUnit</val>,
              <val>souce</val>)</cell>
            <cell>the closed lists' values: a misspelt type fails the RelaxNG</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#text-divisions"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><att>unit</att> of <gi>biblScope</gi> and <gi>citedRange</gi>: <val>tome</val>, <val>vol</val>,
              <val>tomus</val>, <val>band</val>, <val>fascicle</val>, <val>fascicule</val>, <val>heft</val></cell>
            <cell><val>volume</val>, <val>part</val> or <val>issue</val>, by what the edition counts</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#editions-pages"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><gi>gap</gi> with <att>reason</att> <val>missing</val></cell>
            <cell><val>lacuna</val></cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#transcription-gaps"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row role="label">
            <cell cols="3">What is marked in the text</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><gi>note</gi> typed <val>corresp</val>; untyped notes; the old guide's <val>filiation</val>,
              <val>physDesc</val>, <val>warning</val>, <val>comment</val>, <val>memo</val> and <val>desc</val></cell>
            <cell><val>parallel</val>, or <val>reception</val> where the edition gives the later texts that took the
              passage over; <val>editorial</val> or <val>source</val>, by what the note does</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#marked-notes"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>A source note's codes in its words</cell>
            <cell>in its <att>source</att></cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#marked-notes"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Codes in older styles: <code>CNIC.325.2</code>; <code>CanApost_N</code>, <code>Apost_N</code>,
              <code>SEA_N</code>; <code>DCEL.422.369</code>, whose year isn't the file's; pointers to the
              standOff's entries (<code>quote source="#CNIC"</code>)</cell>
            <cell>codes and citations as the coding rules make them: <code>C.NIC-0325_2</code>;
              <code>COLL.CanApost_N</code>, <code>COLL.SEA_N</code>; <code>D.CEL-0428-369</code>, by the table of
              files</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#marked-pointers"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Placeholders without their <code>#</code>, or capitalised</cell>
            <cell><code>#new_person_…</code>, in lower case before the encoder's name</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#records-ids"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>One <gi>quote</gi> around several paragraphs</cell>
            <cell>fragments, one in each paragraph, joined by <att>next</att> and <att>prev</att></cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#marked-fragments"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row role="label">
            <cell cols="3">Records, relations and dates</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>An authority's records as links, in a <gi>note</gi> typed <val>links</val>; its bare numbers, in a
              <gi>note</gi> typed <val>authorities</val></cell>
            <cell><gi>idno</gi> typed by the authority (<code>&lt;idno type="mirabile"&gt;19840&lt;/idno&gt;</code>)</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#records-external-ids"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>Relations after SAWS and the project's own terms, their ends pointing to the standOff's
              entries</cell>
            <cell>the model's relation types, each with its permalink; SAWS's under "is a text of"</cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#relations-types"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><att>calendar</att> <val>Gregorian</val>, undeclared</cell>
            <cell><code>#gregorian</code>, pointing to a <gi>calendar</gi> declared in <gi>calendarDesc</gi></cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#dates-calendars"/></cell>
          </row>
          <row role="label">
            <cell cols="3">Manuscripts</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell>The Bodleian's description: the whole manuscript's physical description and contents;
              <gi>num</gi>; <gi>filiation</gi>; <gi>msItem</gi>/<att>class</att>; an untyped
              <gi>altIdentifier</gi> as a unit's identifier</cell>
            <cell>the guide's description: physical description and contents on the units; <gi>num</gi>'s words
              kept as words; relations between the texts; the unit's own <gi>idno</gi></cell>
            <cell><ptr target="#manuscripts-bodleian"/>, and the table in <ptr target="#appendix-mappings"/></cell>
          </row>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div xml:id="appendix-mappings">
        <head>The import formats</head>
        <p>Others' TEI comes in through its own schema, then a converter into the guide's forms (<ptr
            target="#manuscripts-bodleian"/>). For each format, its table says what the conversion does with each of
          its elements and attributes: keeps it, moves it, makes a record or a relation of it, or drops it, and
          why.</p>
        <xi:include href="mappings/bodleian.xml"/>
      </div>
      <divGen xml:id="appendix-changes" type="changes">
        <head>The changes</head>
      </divGen>
      <div xml:id="example-sources">
        <head>The sources of the examples</head>
        <p>The guide's examples quote short excerpts of the project's corpus, cut where the point is made and revised to
          the forms this guide decides; marks that don't concern the point may be left out. Each example names its
          file here, by
          <att>source</att>: the file's code, the text, and the edition or the manuscript it was transcribed from. An
          example without a source is made up, where the corpus has nothing to show, and so are the
          counter-examples.</p>
        <listBibl>
          <bibl xml:id="source-C.AAC-0816"><idno>C.AAC-0816</idno>: <title>Council of Aachen, 816</title>, ed.
            <editor>Albert Werminghoff</editor>, <title>Concilia aevi Karolini</title> I, MGH Concilia 2.1 (Hannover
            and Leipzig, <date>1906</date>), pp. 307–464.</bibl>
          <bibl xml:id="source-C.AAC-0836"><idno>C.AAC-0836</idno>: <title>Council of Aachen, 836</title>, ed.
            <editor>Albert Werminghoff</editor>, <title>Concilia aevi Karolini</title> II, MGH Concilia 2.2 (Hannover
            and Leipzig, <date>1908</date>), pp. 704–767.</bibl>
